# ANV-0061 -- the coordinator recorded the leader hint every reply carried and
# retried against the node that sent it
#
# Coordinator::send picks its destination from the cached descriptor. Every
# reply carries a leader_hint; on_reply copied it into the response and no
# caller ever read it. So every one of a request's eight attempts went back to
# the replica that had just refused it and named the alternative.
seed        = 1 (bank, snapshot isolation) is the sharpest; it is every seed
workload    = txn_bank, either kind
nodes       = 5
keys        = 16, neighbourhood 4, txns_per_client 16
faults      = drawn from seed. Any lease handover or leadership change is
              enough, which under this phase's churn is constant.
invariant   = none. This is a liveness bug and the measurement is the abort
              rate, which is why it survived every safety gate in the phase.
reproduce   = anvil_txn_faults 30, and read the header line
expect      = before the fix, across 3 levels x 10 seeds:
                108 committed, 1199 aborted
              on seed 1 alone, from the coordinators' own counters:
                begun=321 committed=5 aborted=312 not_leader=1986
              1,986 rejections against 321 transactions is six refusals per
              transaction, each of which named the node to ask instead.
              After the fix: 147 committed, 949 aborted.
witness     = `not_leader` divided by `begun`. The counter had been printed the
              whole time.
note        = api_visible: yes, as an abort rather than a wrong answer -- which
              is why it is S2 and not S0. The consequence was out of proportion
              to the bug because it sat upstream of every measurement the phase
              makes: a mutation drill that scores a deliberate bug by whether an
              anomaly appears cannot score anything when the workload commits
              four transactions a seed. `lost update` went 11/15 to 15/15 on
              this fix alone, with nothing about the mutation or its detector
              changed.
